        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Wet sealer is a water problem: hose, degreaser, brush, done. Cured sealer is a solvent problem: citrus remover or tar remover, dwell, scrub, blot, repeat, and a poultice for the shadow. Never acid on concrete, never solvent on skin, never a brush on car paint.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            The cheapest removal method is tape along the concrete, a brush along the edges, a running hose and old shoes. Set up before the pail opens and there is very little to remove afterwards.
          </p>
        </div>

